          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Billing distinguishes processed bytes from returned and transferred bytes, including transfers between query nodes and writes from $out or $merge. Partitioning only helps processing cost when a query avoids reading irrelevant data; a full scan can still read every partition. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/billing/data-federation/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ca8c2cc92b510d91c3f84429702de133c86f7ca3b3fa241d87300b96585bbe29",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:70215812835ee0b03de4781bfc81b798e6397c8a23b2c07e526deffd0ea843ce"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Partitioning does not reduce scans when a query still needs all data. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/query/query-federated-database.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d1ea08fbed69e117ed2637060b95f2f38b9a83136257aaa45d0890caccdd2c31",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4fb6b00311b0ca5c0e58820a40dcc0d17029338835d13eeac8ad77a472cda483"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/adf-overview/query-performance-optimization.md"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How-to and procedures",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Configure stores and virtual collection mappings through the Atlas UI visual or JSON editor, federation commands, or Atlas Administration API endpoints. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
