    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas Data Federation maps existing data stores into virtual databases and collections; it can query Atlas clusters, S3, Azure Blob Storage and HTTP sources without requiring a consolidated copy first. (medium confidence) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/adf-overview/key-concepts.md ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/adf-overview/key-concepts.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ed7f49fdd11f2e0cb85f20f5258ef164324d93a54cee4c2243b94210feea154e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:586b421f3c1f0dda46c39a4b23af046d093af9abaa4520146d64f1066174a364"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.manning.com/preview/mongodb-in-action-third-edition/chapter-16",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "claim_id": "clm:5e1d2e531a133ef435f61ed0c6acd8b7f6fe4f31469aa60f93d6ae9ce148ef48",
            "outcome": "VERIFIED",
            "at": "2026-11-02T10:41:13Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Data Federation can export aggregation results through $out to Amazon S3 in formats including CSV, BSON and Parquet; the Data Federation $out stage is a distinct variant with its own s3 settings. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/supported-unsupported/pipeline/out.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/supported-unsupported/pipeline/out.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c64595ff8e957c7962fa4addf47e11c852747b3a7ed9ad65c1756b14e2ce4d4f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:14a7260f92797f12690667df4d743f3d130196508d54d80c631a1c4ae1b67fb6"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://studio3t.com/download-resources/ebooks/3t_guide_to_aggregation.pdf"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "claim_id": "clm:d93372a394671232d04522e8b8d546d07c2d4feec1a53e6e6e3ff82c26c3f7c6",
            "outcome": "CORRECTED",
            "at": "2026-11-02T10:41:13Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Veezoo connects through the Atlas SQL Interface backed by a federated instance. Its setup uses the JDBC hostname and virtual database name; this Veezoo integration requires an Atlas cluster. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)",
          "source": "https://docs.veezoo.com/veezoo/getting-started/database-connections/mongodb-atlas",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:16acb57c00d08abeae84b78b9ddff0035c0652685bccf03be12744d5cd40ed19",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e5f660ede081d21a403cb53a3e111fc073aa4ba51cbd70790d03385f45d9e278"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Veezoo warns that sampled SQL schemas can mishandle polymorphic fields and that nested documents and arrays need flattened views for import. Its guide recommends sqlSetSchema or regenerating stale schemas with sqlGenerateSchema. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)",
          "source": "https://docs.veezoo.com/veezoo/getting-started/database-connections/mongodb-atlas",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c5cc5a63a770fb12181c3f7334d48e890ec26e69ac570ca6d5280523e229017c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:283724bd5fbc32ccfa473b906e3243b6dde13513677993707d4d5291afe659c2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Federation does not provide full MongoDB server parity: creating indexes on federated sources, change streams, and multi-document ACID transactions are unsupported. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/supported-unsupported/limitations.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b06c0e3de53f945b689359c91244846a4b6d02befa91d1c2219d5d972baf2092",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:daad405267d861085e7807a7d163a8892ac4ac114e8492b6fb37924fde2c4a9d"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A federated database instance can use object storage from only one cloud provider and one account within that provider; the instance itself runs in a specific cloud and region. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/supported-unsupported/limitations.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d9c4c9bc91254b0b45a2015b3e5e012720001f52e434b13195ba8a036a02297a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a1ac76e7a6c8e5ea270d27f5163b2f193373de1334d4eda689517c62b7a2b4e6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "SERVER-104844 records a historical provisioning bug: CreateFederatedDatabase could return HTTP 200 for an overly long generated hostname, while subsequent DNS lookup and connection failed. The ticket was resolved on May 8, 2025; it does not establish a current defect. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-104844",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:869fe10fb854f0aacb91cbd7b40c513188ea1d6c58e93dd95640bdb9c9cc6750",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6a99d66455d516fb8506f1135f1d64b66cbeecf3ac22314917dc82b15a775460"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas Data Federation represents underlying stores as virtual databases and collections, enabling queries across Atlas clusters and external data without first consolidating everything into one physical collection. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/query/query-federated-database.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:af36a5c8307c4a2d83169cbe63b6aae3fd90a3bf4f564d84ac468da1e72df602",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6387db3de8a80e214fcecdcd038087c1a6f9afe470233aa071190a937cc3b658"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.manning.com/preview/mongodb-in-action-third-edition/chapter-16"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Supported query sources documented here include Atlas clusters, Amazon S3, Azure Blob Storage, Google Cloud Storage, and files at public HTTP/HTTPS URLs. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/query/query-federated-database.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c1dad8fa0255bffb0e0c5bca30a5a16a7fb3f8318c800801899fb4b8a7cce9f2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:609f7d555faa46a1111f383cf8cb528cfc746ab24e1b7bb7d6c9e763d361cf43"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MongoDB-compatible clients can query a federated database instance. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/data-federation/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:717438bdcee677fb4d73896881b3c877b195afb396a878ed30146a74d001c95f",
